EXEMPLAR — the paragraph transport-security-setup writes into the root CLAUDE.md, right below the
`**Bounded context:` paragraph (or below the first heading when there is none). One of the two
bodies, with its placeholders filled. This template owns the wording; the skill's entry rule
greps for `**Transport:` to know the project already decided.
-->

**Transport: topology A — TLS terminates at the edge.** The application holds no key and trusts
`X-Forwarded-*` only from `TRUSTED_PROXIES`; HSTS is written by the application, never by the
edge. Norms: `.claude/rules/transport-security.md`. {{localEdge}}

**Transport: topology B — the embedded server terminates TLS{{mtls}}.** Certificate and key are
mounted at run time from `TLS_CERTIFICATE` / `TLS_PRIVATE_KEY`, served on 8443 and reloaded on
change; the profiles {{plainProfiles}} run plain HTTP on 8080. Reason: {{reason}}. Norms:
`.claude/rules/transport-security.md`, `.claude/rules/secrets.md`.
